Cell["\<\
The tree mirrors what PathToTreePath gave numerically: every internal node is \
a binary merge of two subtrees, the leaves are the input tensors, and the \
root is the final result. Reading from leaves to root recovers the exact \
step-by-step plan that the engine will execute when the expression is \
activated. The mathematical relationship between the path, the tree, and the \
final Inactive expression is: the path is a positional schedule, the tree \
records which tensors meet at which nodes, and the Inactive expression is the \
same tree decorated with the specific back-end primitives \[Dash] \
Inactive[ArrayDot], Inactive[Transpose], and friends \[Dash] that the chosen \
Method will execute. Three views, one plan.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8030f017-ba04-4b37-832c-2d1737e309b5"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["6. The Five Contraction Engines", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"54b7e484-4c43-4b25-8fa1-04a4124d90d5"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Once a path is fixed, the remaining choice is which numerical primitive \
turns a pair of tensors into their contraction. The paclet ships five \
interchangeable engines, listed in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["$TensorNetworkContractionMethods",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->
    "paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/$TensorNetworkContractionMethods"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"84c274f8-3915-42d5-bcaf-530e3b801490"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d2d379ae-8302-40ba-84e4-3625a9b68a8a"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData["$TensorNetworkContractionMethods"], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[185]:=",ExpressionUUID->"e27a9039-a314-428a-9a2e-d6b2f5b4ad3a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"\<\"ArrayDotTranspose\"\>", ",", "\<\"ArrayDot\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"Dot\"\>", ",", "\<\"TensorContract\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"TableSum\"\>"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.988065428383214*^9, 3.988065543541484*^9, 
  3.988116135460154*^9, 3.988224814221006*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[185]=",
 CellID->29491151,ExpressionUUID->"b1ef2d1b-ae32-4b4a-888e-3b559c2a1ddc"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each engine implements the same mathematical operation \[Dash] a pairwise \
contraction \[Dash] but with a different internal representation. ",
 "\"ArrayDot\"",
 " is the default: it sorts shared axes, calls the optimized ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["ArrayDot",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/ArrayDot"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "3dca6ee3-843f-461a-99c9-dec612419a24"],
 " primitive directly, and is fastest for dense tensors. ",
 "\"ArrayDotTranspose\"",
 " inserts explicit ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Transpose",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Transpose"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "669be6da-793d-48ac-8b31-f4f619e215b4"],
 " nodes to align indices before the dot \[Dash] slightly larger expression \
trees but identical numerics. ",
 "\"Dot\"",
 " reshapes both tensors into matrices and falls back to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Dot",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Dot"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "53c763ef-dae7-4da2-be39-6f79e5828fb9"],
 "; useful when an external Dot has been customized or accelerated. ",
 "\"TensorContract\"",
 " expresses the merge as a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["TensorContract",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/TensorContract"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "5deaefdb-d7eb-42ca-bf0d-332c65fc179b"],
 " over a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["TensorProduct",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/TensorProduct"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "72364d86-177b-45ed-b020-43cd86507d1d"],
 "; closest to a textbook \"contract these slots\" specification but rarely \
the fastest. ",
 "\"TableSum\"",
 " builds an explicit ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Table",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Table"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "a6515d0d-42a8-49c0-9044-36bbbcb0b86c"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Sum",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Sum"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "b7456e96-ec0f-473b-8b56-82ae3fdc93b5"],
 " over the contracted indices; semantically transparent but quadratically \
slower."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"753964cd-5944-4510-8630-633af303171e"],

Cell["\<\
The distinction matters because the same pairwise contraction can be coded \
several ways, and the cost of the inner kernel \[Dash] not just the \
contraction order \[Dash] affects wall-clock time. Two networks with \
identical optimal paths will run at very different speeds if one is \
contracted with \"ArrayDot\" and the other with \"TableSum\". A useful mental \
model: the planner decides what gets contracted together, the engine decides \
how. To compare two engines, build a small numeric network and contract it \
twice:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6ce5e16f-c09f-435a-898e-6621661b1c49"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Reproducibility \[Dash] set a fixed seed before drawing random tensors.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fb4895d0-5a16-43ee-ad6f-ac312d216f72"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "7", "]"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[186]:=",ExpressionUUID->"e5277889-3ee5-487c-9276-e8148d8f548d"]
}, Open  ]],

